===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|ota|آذربایجان|tr=Azerbaycan}}, from {{der|en|fa-cls|آذَرْبَایْجَان|tr=āḏarbāyjān, āzarbāyjān}}, Arabized form of Early {{m+|fa-cls|آذَرْبَایْگَان|tr=āḏarbāygān, āzarbāygān}} / {{m|fa-cls|آذَرْبَادْگَان|tr=āḏarbādgān, āzarbādgān}}, from {{der|en|pal|tr=ʾtwrpʾtkʾn}} / {{m|pal|tr=ʾtwrpʾtkn|ts=Āturpātakān, Ādurbādagān}},<ref>{{cite book|last=Schippmann|first=K.|year=1987|chapter=AZERBAIJAN iii. Pre-Islamic History|title=Encyclopædia Iranica|url=https://www.iranicaonline.org/articles/azerbaijan-iii|passage=The Middle Persian form of the name was (early) Āturpātakān, (later) Ādurbādagān {{…}}}}</ref> from {{m|pal|tr=ʾtwrpʾt'|ts=Āturpāt, Ādurbād⁠|t={{w|Atropates}} (the Persian nobleman who founded the kingdom of [[Atropatene]])}} [whose name descends from {{der|en|peo|*Ātr̥pātah|lit=protected by fire}}] {{suf|pal|nocat=1||-kʾn'}} (whence {{m+|fa-cls|ـگَان}}).

Compare {{cog|xcl|Ատրպատական}}, {{m|xcl|Ատրապատական}}, {{m|xcl|Ատրպայական}}, {{cog|hy|Ադրբեջան}}, {{cog|gkm|Ἀδαρβιγάνων}}, {{cog|syc|ܐܕܘܪܒܝܓܐܢ|tr=ʾĀḏōrbêḡān}}, {{cog|cop|ⲁⲇⲟⲩⲣⲃⲁⲇⲁⲅⲁⲛ|}}.

